text='# Phase 2S full representation coverage benchmark\n\n## Final gate\n\n`'+verdict+'`\n\nSPPIDER_RESCUE_STATUS = '+rescue(sp)+'; XPAIR_RESCUE_STATUS = '+rescue(xp)+'. These are interface-representation availability outcomes, not variant-specific disruption or disease prediction.\n\n'
text+='## Frozen inputs and historical result\n\n124/124 frozen files passed SHA256 verification before inference and again at finalization. U1=42, U2=132, frozen gene–partner pairs=15,942; canonical sequences=7,300/7,300; common-primary membership=9,978. Historical MutPred remains 9 genes ≥70% and 3 balanced genes (FGFR2, MEN1, TUBA1A). Common-denominator comparisons below are new quantities and do not rewrite the historical output.\n\n'
text+='## Prespecified methods\n\n'+rd('results/phase2S_full/run_manifest.tsv').to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\nAll sequence inference used exact WT proteins and unchanged official neural heads. SPPIDER receptor output is primary and peptide output remains separately cached. Windowing is1024 tokens/stride512, with full query and context. X-PAIR requires50–2000 residues in both proteins; unsupported proteins were not truncated and interaction probability did not filter interface output. X-PAIR caches preserve the official six-decimal raw export before the CLI rounds its presentation file to three decimals. Exact offline loader diffs and environments are available in Phase2SR.\n\n'
text+='## Denominators and balance\n\nGene C4 uses exactly the common-primary registry for every arm: variants with ≥3 distinct frozen credible partner scores divided by the frozen primary denominator. Raw fractions are thresholded at0.70 before rounding. Disease-group denominators and mapped membership follow recovered legacy logic. All strict ≥10 groups enter the legacy coverage range; retaining ≥2 groups with ≥10 unambiguous variants is a separate balance eligibility gate. Severe imbalance uses minimum<0.50 or range≥0.50; material uses range≥0.20 or straddling0.70; minor is the remainder. Original legacy score-row-conditioned multilabel behavior is preserved in U1, including674 multilabel variants absent from score rows that remain in its primary denominator.\n\n'
text+='## Full representation coverage\n\n'+summary.to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\nCounts evaluate availability, including genuine zero interface probabilities; unavailable observations are never zero-filled. Pair-space coverage and variant GE3 coverage have separate denominators. New structural arms use finite original distance or explicitly supported original binary assignments; no structure was regenerated.\n\n'
text+='## Pair status and length constraints\n\n'+causes.to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\n'+length.to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\nLong-query SPPIDER technical coverage is recorded in sppider_long_sequence_audit.tsv. Lower X-PAIR coverage due to length constraints is an input-contract result, not evidence of biological inferiority.\n\n'
text+='## Rescued genes\n\n'+rc.loc[rc[['SPPIDER_RESCUED','XPAIR_RESCUED','BOTH_RESCUED','SEQUENCE_ONLY_RESCUED']].any(axis=1)].to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\nRescue is relative to the historical three-gene MutPred balanced set. Sequence-only requires all three structure-dependent arms to fail their common-denominator balanced gate.\n\n'
text+='## Secondary consensus\n\nAvailability consensus requires both valid same-position scores. Continuous consensus standardizes each model globally over shared common-primary variant–partner rows using populationSD, fixed before full outcomes. Parameters are in consensus_standardization_parameters.json. CONSENSUS_HIGH_SECONDARY requires both probabilities≥0.5 for ≥3 partners. Neither secondary arm replaces the individual primary outcomes.\n\n'
text+='## Experimental structural validity\n\n'+val.to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\nLabels use frozen experimental biological-assembly heavy-atom contacts≤5Å only; unobserved residues and predicted PIONEER labels were excluded. The evaluation unit is residue×query-partner pair; repeated assemblies are merged into one union contact label per unit. Micro metrics pool eligible units. Macro metrics average per-query protein estimates. Bootstrap resamples query proteins1000 times, seed20261003, and retains their entire residue/pair clusters. One-class protein AUROC/AUPRC are explicitly unevaluable. SPPIDER/X-PAIR training overlap has not been established; these are internal structural validity estimates, not independent held-out performance.\n\n'
text+='## Partner specificity and shuffled controls\n\n'+specific.to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\nPairwise Spearman/Pearson values are available for all scored partner tracks of queries with≥3 partners. Meaningful dispersion was frozen as per-residue across-partner populationSD≥0.05. Constant tracks have undefined correlations. The shuffled control selected20 lexicographic sequence-supported genes per method and three frozen partners per gene before inspecting full outcomes. Replacement proteins come from the same frozen length bin, excluding the query and every credible partner of that query. Selection, hashes and track changes are preserved in shuffled_control_plan.tsv and shuffled_partner_control.tsv. No disease label was used.\n\n'
text+='## Technical failure architecture\n\nUnivariable effects summarize technical failure versus success. Multivariable logistic models use at most three prespecified technical predictors and require at least10 minority events per variable; nonidentifiable/separated fits are withheld. Disease identity and phenotype association statistics never enter a model. Variant and pair summaries are descriptive and do not assume independent variants within a gene. Results are in failure_predictor_models.tsv and failure_stage_descriptive_effects.tsv.\n\n'
text+='## Computational resources\n\n'+cost.to_markdown(index=False)+'\n\nSPPIDER timings include encoder/cache IO. X-PAIR batch-allocation proxies are distinguished from measured forward times. MPS GPU busy hours and peakVRAM are NA when unsupported by profiling; they are not reconstructed from elapsed wall time. Frozen baselines incur no new inference cost; original generation cost is not invented.\n\n'
text+='## Figures and tables\n\nFiguresS1–S6 are provided as editableSVG and PNG under results/phase2S_full/figures. Source data are the corresponding TSVs. TableS1–S9 have explicit TSV outputs. FigureS1 uses132 genes and descriptive attrition counts; S2 is alphabetic, not phenotype-ordered; S3 is paired withinU1; S4 distinguishes historical versus common-denominator values; S5 uses macro estimates and1000 protein bootstrap95%CIs; S6 compares technical features descriptively. No hypothesis test or multiple-testing claim accompanies descriptive panels. Final rendered visual QA remains an agent review step before publication use.\n\n'
text+='## Stop and interpretation\n\nOriginal NO_GO_EDGETIC_REPRESENTATION was not altered.\n\nDisease-label phenotype association testing was NOT started.\n\nPhase2P was NOT started.\n\nFull Phase2S computations end here. Any phenotype-information test requires new manual authorization.\n'
report=R/'reports/PHASE2S_FULL_REPRESENTATION_COVERAGE_BENCHMARK.md';report.write_text(text)
(O/'final_gate.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(verdict=verdict,SPPIDER_RESCUE_STATUS=rescue(sp),XPAIR_RESCUE_STATUS=rescue(xp),original_verdict='NO_GO_EDGETIC_REPRESENTATION',SPPIDER_balanced=sp,XPAIR_balanced=xp,completed_at=now(),full_phase2S_computations_completed=True,figure_visual_QA='AGENT_REVIEW_PENDING',phase2P_started=False),indent=2)+'\n');print(verdict,flush=True)
